      "wanneer": "2026-10-28T16:02:43+00:00",
      "gebeurtenis": "teruggestuur",
      "rede": "HERSIEN",
      "bron": "feite",
      "siklus": 1,
      "punte": [
        "[feite] Niemand kan alles wat hy nodig het self maak, plant of myn n — corrected: The sentence says it is impossible for anyone to make, grow or mine everything they need ('Niemand kan ... nie'). That is an absolute that overstates. Self-sufficient living is rare and hard, but people have done it. Narrow the quantifier, not the point: for example, almost nobody makes everything they need themselves, or most people cannot. The lesson's reason for trade, that people specialise and then depend on one another, stays exactly as it is. The title 'Niemand maak alles self nie' carries the same absolute about practice rather than ability. In practice it holds far more closely, but the writer should decide whether the title matches the narrowed sentence."
      ]
